From b804ce4e34a03132476590e19e610b772ccf8cbc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tylnexttime <tylnexttime@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 07:49:21 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Marian M1.1 exactness: per-group slot floor for the
 slot-map path (C-24, C-10)

M1.0 found that at --moe-cache-mib 4000 the three IQ1_M layers of Swift (one
cache group) had 181 slots, fewer than a 19-28 token prompt step selects
(n_tokens x n_expert_used). get_slot_map then sent those steps off the cache
path, and below the op offload batch size (32) their host experts were
computed on the CPU: 3 prompt steps, 3 of 10 greedy answers changed.

Every group now gets, before the rest of the budget is split,
  n_floor = min(min(n_ubatch, 32) * n_expert_used, n_expert)
slots: the distinct experts of one layer that the largest ubatch on the
slot-map path can select (32 = max_batch). A group whose share by bytes is
below its floor is held at the floor and the other groups split the rest by
bytes, so the split is unchanged whenever no floor binds. If the budget of a
device cannot cover the floors, the constructor throws with the minimum
--moe-cache-mib, instead of upstream's silent "not cached" (which also
computes on the CPU). Per-group slots, MiB and floor are logged at load
(INFO); a group held at its floor is logged as a WARN. A WARN also notes
--no-op-offload, under which large ubatches compute host experts on the CPU.

Swift 1.5 IQ2_XS, n_ubatch 512: floor 320 slots per group, 1,223 MiB for the
three floors; the floor binds below about 7,066 MiB (IQ1_M group).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
